nja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T17:14:34-07:00","id":998952,"title":"","content":"What's an Erubian?<br /> <br /> (Don't want to sound like Banky Edwards here, but\u2026)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T18:03:43-07:00","id":998966,"title":"","content":"Non-canonical Exalt type that I first made during the playtest. About as strong as a Dragon-Blooded but a lot harder to kill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T21:25:17-07:00","id":999055,"title":"","content":"Some sort of Exigent then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T21:33:55-07:00","id":999059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1837-show-us-your-commissions-2-the-revenge?p=999055#post999055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some sort of Exigent then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Exigents aren't the only possible non-canonical Exalted, and are something very specific, when an existing lesser deity petitions the Unconquered Sun to grant a mortal power. Other lineages of heroes, other spirits on the stature of the Incarnae, etc. wouldn't be producing Exigents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T17:24:26-08:00","id":1000035,"title":"","content":"No. It's not the Exigence.<br /> I don't know where her Exaltation originally came from (the original creator is no longer in the picture) just that her former masters found it in some dark corner of the world forgotten by time and harnessed it. Lioness is welcome to give it an origin if she likes, but in the context of Nileen's backstory it's unimportant.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T05:27:57-08:00","id":1006141,"title":"","content":"Portrait of an Earth Aspect from my ongoing Southern game, called Mithras. Inspired by Roland from King's <i>The Dark Tower</i>. Both his white jade flame piece and his prayer beads (whose beads are bullet-shaped) are artifacts, though only the latter has Evocations, relating to recalling memories and meditation, mostly.<br /> Rather challenging as far as drawings go for me; I'm not used to drawing detailed weapons or armor, and Mithras is older-looking than the characters I usually draw; rather happy with the way this turned out.<br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/zZExF2k.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":519,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","user":"ChairKicker","date":". 11-21-2016, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T06:03:33-08:00","id":1006157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div cla